                  "type": "concept",
                  "title": "Three Eras: Paper, Hybrid, Electronic",
                  "content": "Health information systems didn't jump from paper to digital overnight. They moved through three distinct eras, and you will still encounter all three in modern practice.\n\n• **Paper era (pre-2000s)**: The legal medical record was a physical chart. HIM departments owned chart rooms, deficiency analysis, and chart-pull request queues. Loss rates of **5-15%** were typical.\n\n• **Hybrid era (~2000-2015)**: Some data lived electronically (lab results, imaging) while progress notes, consent forms, and signatures stayed on paper. The chart was split across systems — a documentation nightmare for release of information.\n\n• **Electronic era (~2015-present)**: The legal record is the **EHR**, with scanned indexed documents for any remaining paper artifacts. Hybrid records still exist for older episodes of care and during downtime events.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">THREE ERAS OF THE MEDICAL RECORD</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">You will still touch all three in your career</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"170\" width=\"940\" height=\"240\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"220\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">PAPER ERA (PRE-2000s)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"265\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Physical chart = the legal medical record</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"300\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">HIM owned chart rooms, deficiency analysis, pulls</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"335\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">5-15% loss / misfile rates were typical</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"375\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Dictation, transcription, handwritten orders, paper MAR</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"430\" width=\"940\" height=\"240\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"480\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">HYBRID ERA (2000-2015)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"525\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Lab and imaging electronic; notes still on paper</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"560\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Documentation split across systems</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"595\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Hardest era for release of information (ROI)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"635\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Legal record definition becomes a compliance project</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"690\" width=\"940\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"740\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">ELECTRONIC ERA (2015 ONWARD)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"785\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">EHR is the legal record of care</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"820\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Paper artifacts scanned + indexed in document mgmt</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"855\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Downtime procedures generate hybrid episodes</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"895\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">HIM pivots to data integrity, governance, analytics</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"935\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Old paper records continue under retention schedules</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "The three-era arc of clinical documentation"
                  }
