                  "explanation": "**45 CFR 164.530(j)** requires covered entities to retain HIPAA documentation (policies, procedures, complaint records, sanctions, training, and access management documentation) for **6 years from the date of its creation or the date when it last was in effect, whichever is later**. While the audit log retention period is not explicitly numbered, OCR enforcement aligns to this 6-year minimum, and most health systems retain audit logs for 7–10 years to align with state medical record retention laws (Texas requires 7 years for adult records).",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">HIPAA Retention: 6 Years</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\" text-anchor=\"middle\">45 CFR 164.530(j) documentation rule</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"180\" width=\"1000\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The Six-Year Clock</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"310\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Retain 6 years from the date of creation</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"355\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">OR the date the document was last in effect</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"400\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">- whichever is LATER.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"460\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Applies to policies, procedures, complaints,</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"495\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">training records, sanctions, access logs.</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"600\" width=\"500\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"660\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\">Federal Minimum</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"720\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">HIPAA = 6 years</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"770\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">documentation retention.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"830\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">OCR audit baseline.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"890\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Note: medical record</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"920\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">retention is state law.</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"600\" width=\"480\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"660\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\">Texas Standard</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"720\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Adult records: 7 years</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"755\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">after last treatment.</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"810\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Minor records: age of</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"845\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">majority plus statute.</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"900\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Most systems align audit</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"925\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">logs to chart retention.</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "HIPAA mandates 6-year retention; state law (Texas: 7 years adult) often extends it further."
                  }
