                  "explanation": "**RPO (Recovery POINT Objective)** is the maximum acceptable **data loss** — here, 15 minutes — which dictates backup frequency. **RTO (Recovery TIME Objective)** is the maximum acceptable **downtime** — here, 4 hours — which dictates DR architecture (probably a warm or hot site for EHR). The mnemonic 'P = Past data; T = Time down' helps you remember which is which.",
